        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "502dc444-409c-510f-973d-0858bfda9bf3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Earl Holding, Harry F. Sinclair, Georg Hochfilzer\n- Companies: Sinclair Oil Corporation, Sinclair Oil and Refining Corporation\n- Products: Little America Hotels, Grand America Hotel, Westgate Hotel\n- Places: San Diego, California, central Idaho, Ogden, Utah\n- Projects: Sun Valley, Snowbasin\n\nFacts:\n- Harry F. Sinclair founded Sinclair Oil and Refining Corporation on May 1, 1916, by combining the assets of 11 small petroleum companies.\n- Sinclair Oil Corporation is an American petroleum corporation.\n- Robert Earl Holding was born on November 29, 1926, and was an American businessman.\n- Robert Earl Holding owned Sinclair Oil Corporation.\n- Robert Earl Holding owned Little America Hotels, the Grand America Hotel, and the Westgate Hotel in San Diego, California.\n- Georg Hochfilzer directed the Westgate Hotel in San Diego, California.\n- Robert Earl Holding owned Sun Valley in central Idaho from 1977.\n- Robert Earl Holding owned Snowbasin near Ogden, Utah, from 1984.\n- Robert Earl Holding died on April 19, 2013.",
